conf: --no-neigh-notify, to run without the neighbour listener

passt subscribes to the host's neighbour table (nl_neigh_notify_init(): a
NETLINK_ROUTE socket bound to RTMGRP_NEIGH) and mirrors the MAC addresses
it learns into the frames it sends the guest. The kernel visits every
NETLINK_ROUTE multicast socket on the host for each link and neighbour
notification of any network namespace, under rtnl_mutex
(netlink_broadcast_filtered() -> do_one_broadcast()), so a host with
thousands of pasta instances pays for thousands of listeners on every link
change of every one of them: with 2000 instances do_one_broadcast() was
8% of all samples under a TAP's attach and detach.

With the option passt does not open that socket. fwd_neigh_mac_get() finds
no entry and falls back to passt's own MAC address, which is what passt
sent before it had the table.

Carried by fcvm for its pooled namespaces. Not submitted upstream yet.

diff --git a/conf.c b/conf.c
index 8205dbf..ecb50d7 100644
--- a/conf.c
+++ b/conf.c
@@ -662,6 +662,7 @@ static void usage(const char *name, FILE *f, int status)
 		"  --no-icmp		Disable ICMP/ICMPv6 protocol handler\n"
 		"  --no-dhcp		Disable DHCP server\n"
 		"  --no-ndp		Disable NDP responses\n"
+		"  --no-neigh-notify	Don't follow the host's neighbour table\n"
 		"  --no-dhcpv6		Disable DHCPv6 server\n"
 		"  --no-ra		Disable router advertisements\n"
 		"  --freebind		Bind to any address for forwarding\n"
@@ -1297,6 +1298,7 @@ void conf(struct ctx *c, int argc, char **argv)
 		{"no-dhcp",	no_argument,		&c->no_dhcp,	1 },
 		{"no-dhcpv6",	no_argument,		&c->no_dhcpv6,	1 },
 		{"no-ndp",	no_argument,		&c->no_ndp,	1 },
+		{"no-neigh-notify", no_argument,	&c->no_neigh,	1 },
 		{"no-ra",	no_argument,		&c->no_ra,	1 },
 		{"no-splice",	no_argument,		&c->no_splice,	1 },
 		{"splice-only",	no_argument,		&c->splice_only, 1 },
diff --git a/passt.1 b/passt.1
index 995590a..e72516a 100644
--- a/passt.1
+++ b/passt.1
@@ -352,6 +352,14 @@ selected IPv4 default route.
 Disable Neighbor Discovery. NDP messages coming from guest or target
 namespace will be ignored. No initial NDP message will be sent.
 
+.TP
+.BR \-\-no-neigh-notify
+Do not subscribe to the host's neighbour table. Frames for the guest then carry
+passt's own MAC address as their source, whichever host sent them. Every
+listener of this kind is visited, under the host's rtnl lock, by each link and
+neighbour notification of any network namespace, so a host that runs thousands
+of instances can turn it off.
+
 .TP
 .BR \-\-no-dhcpv6
 Disable the DHCPv6 server. DHCPv6 client requests coming from guest or target
diff --git a/passt.c b/passt.c
index 5054551..ad8703f 100644
--- a/passt.c
+++ b/passt.c
@@ -421,7 +421,8 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
 	pcap_init(c);
 
 	fwd_neigh_table_init(c);
-	nl_neigh_notify_init(c);
+	if (!c->no_neigh)
+		nl_neigh_notify_init(c);
 
 	if (isolate_prefork(c))
 		die("Failed to sandbox process, exiting");
diff --git a/passt.h b/passt.h
index a61baca..a6de22f 100644
--- a/passt.h
+++ b/passt.h
@@ -208,6 +208,7 @@ struct ip6_ctx {
  * @no_dhcp:		Disable DHCP server
  * @no_dhcpv6:		Disable DHCPv6 server
  * @no_ndp:		Disable NDP handler altogether
+ * @no_neigh:		Don't listen for the host's neighbour events
  * @no_ra:		Disable router advertisements
  * @no_splice:		Disable socket splicing for inbound traffic
  * @splice_only:	Only enable loopback forwarding
@@ -293,6 +294,7 @@ struct ctx {
 	int no_dhcp;
 	int no_dhcpv6;
 	int no_ndp;
+	int no_neigh;
 	int no_ra;
 	int no_splice;
 	int splice_only;
